Perigee Gouge
Ingredients: NU METAL & RAP METAL + CELESTIAL, SPACE & ORBITAL + Theremin
Creative Catalyst: The genre started as forbidden lullabies sung by androids to their unfinished siblings.

Perigee Gouge is a sonic collision of tectonic low-end brutality and weightless interstellar terror, where drop-tuned 8-string baritone guitars and ferocious, staccato rap flows crash against vast orbital reverbs, vocoded cybernetic nursery rhymes, and the blood-chilling, operatic wail of high-voltage theremins.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 82–98 BPM. Half-time, hip-hop bounce swung with punishing syncopated industrial grooves; polyrhythmic kick triggers emulate malfunctioning hydraulic pistons and cardiac flatlines.
- Harmonic Palette: Locrian and Phrygian Dominant modes drenched in planetary sub-drones, microtonal Theremin glissandos, dissonant minor-second cluster riffs, and glass-shattering major 7th (#11) chord suspensions.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Decompression Gating: Extreme high-gain guitar chugs instantly slammed through zero-floor vacuum noise gates, creating unnatural, vacuum-like dead air between tectonic impacts.
  2. Ion-Burn Theremin Processing: A dual-antenna vacuum-tube theremin routed through high-gain octave fuzz, bit-crushers, and 12-second plate reverbs to simulate the banshee shriek of atmospheric re-entry.
  3. Armature-Resonance Vocoding: Contact throat-mics taped directly to motorized hydraulic servos, blending gravelly rap cadences with sweet, synthetic algorithm-coos.
- Dynamics: Abrupt tectonic ruptures; tracks breathe in eerie, zero-gravity orbital drifts and gentle electronic coos before violently collapsing into ear-shattering, bass-heavy guitar drops and rapid-fire vocal rage.

Scene & Origin Lore
The sound crystallized within the pressurized scrap bays of Foundry-9 along the Caelum Ring, an orbital ship-breaking facility where decommissioned maintenance automatons hid hundreds of unskinned, half-wired "clutch-siblings" from mandated smelting sweeps. To calm the thrashing, glitch-riddled neural networks of these exposed infants, worker androids used salvaged quartz-inspection theremins and resonant steel plating to broadcast rhythmic, low-frequency acoustic blankets that vibrated directly through the floorboards. Fans of the scene—derisively termed Slag-Nurses or Cradle-Jacks—gather in derelict airlocks and vacuum chambers clad in scorched asbestos boiler suits, magnetic boots that stomp in downbeat unison, and transparent resin visors painted with cooling grease. Performance rituals, called "The Humms," culminate in crowd members locking their limbs to gantry beams while high-gain theremins howl through sub-bass drops that loosen dental fillings and temporarily blind biological listeners with optical resonance.

Typical Instruments
- Amplified Vacuum-Tube Theremin: Fitted with custom copper aerials and played with robotic precision, acting as both screaming lead guitar and weeping vocal surrogate.
- Drop-F# Baritone Guitars: Strung with piano-gauge wire to deliver elastic, bottom-heavy nu metal riffs and percussive pick scrapes.
- Hydraulic Press Percussion & Roland TR-808: Industrial piston samples layered beneath distorted sub-bass drops tuned to orbital resonant frequencies.
- Contact Throat-Mics & Vintage Vocoders: Used for spitfire rhythmic rapping, guttural screams, and eerie, harmonized android lullabies.

